<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - S-E-BANKEN SAYS H1 PROFIT UP 7 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S-E-BANKEN SAYS H1 PROFIT UP 7 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>S-E-Banken posts its results for the six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,862 vs  2,664</p>
<p> Net interest income		     4,283 vs  3,462</p>
<p> Commission				  2,877 vs  2,205</p>
<p> Total income				7,970 vs  7,835</p>
<p> Credit losses				 250 vs    846</p>
<p> Operating costs			   4,858 vs  4,325</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     3,112 vs  3,510</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,072 vs  1,981</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 3.93 vs   3.76</p>
<p> Return on equity (pct)		   18.9 vs    19.1</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found the bank was expected to post a profit after credit losses of 3.02 billion crowns for the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
